      "writtenOn": "2018-11-21T10:18:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The intent of this CL to fix the *correctness* bug; kryo385 is not a cortex-a75 and doesn\u0027t have DOT_PRODUCT instruction features (this will result into SIGILL when trying to execute related instructions).\n\nI\u0027ve put a53 from the best of my knowledge and as a conservative option; I believe it is better than to put \"generic\" cpu variant.\n\nIn a future CL one could experiment on fine tuning and optimizations, it would be great if Qualcomm engineers were involved.",
      "parentUuid": "b9fbf1c4_52a770f0",
      "revId": "7836cd84c51dd856c680cfa6478ae66afd97bc48",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c845c6ea_1ba14216",
        "filename": "cc/config/arm_device.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 156,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308278
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-21T15:56:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Is cortex-a53 actually the best choice? Did we ask the CPU architects\n\u003e for their suggested flags?\n\nIt is a question to Clang/LLVM compiler engineers.\nFrom my knowledge of Clang/LLVM, when a correct \u0027march\u0027 is used, a particular \u0027mcpu\u0027 can provide additional information for tuning, e.g. enable an instruction scheduler. What I see in the LLVM sources Cortex-A55/A75 are mostly modelled with Cortex-A53/A57. Of course, this can be changed in the future.\nI think the best solution would be if Qualcomm engineers add support of kryo385 to Clang/LLVM. At the moment Clang/LLVM supports only kryo (Snapdragon 820). I don\u0027t know why Qualcomm has not upstreamed the support of kryo385 yet.\nBTW Clang/LLVM supports the latest Samsung Exynos M3.",
      "parentUuid": "491dc909_13b311a7",
      "revId": "7836cd84c51dd856c680cfa6478ae66afd97bc48",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a980dc93_283960d2",
        "filename": "cc/config/arm_device.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 157,
